## The 20× mirage: how naive microbenchmarks inflate WebGPU’s true cost

A paper from February 2026 — “Characterizing WebGPU Dispatch Overhead for LLM Inference” (arXiv:2604.02344) — set out to answer a deceptively simple question: what does a single WebGPU dispatch actually cost? The authors measured across four GPU vendors (NVIDIA, AMD, Apple, Intel), two native implementations (Dawn and wgpu-native), three browsers, and two model sizes (Qwen2.5-0.5B and 1.5B). Their headline finding is uncomfortable for anyone who has benchmarked WebGPU by wrapping a single operation in a timer (per the paper’s abstract): naive single-operation benchmarks overestimate dispatch cost by roughly 20×.

The mechanism is a measurement artifact the authors call sync conflation. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
